course: dictionary
lesson: 4598
title: Heritage: what we pass on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Heritage is one of those words. In «World Heritage Site», it names a place that is old and protected because it is important. Read the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: Heritage can also mean the culture and background you get from your family. When someone talks about their «Polish heritage», they mean the traditions and history their family brings with them. The word looks back at the past, but people use it with pride today.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «The fish have been kept in the rice fields for over 1,200 years», the idea is something passed on for a very long time. If your swapped meaning still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Heritage means the history, traditions, buildings, art and language that a country or group has had for a long time and passes on.
fact: Your heritage is the culture and background you get from your family and ancestors.
fact: «Heritage railway» means an old railway line that is protected because it is important.
fact: In 2022 UNESCO listed Ukrainian borscht cooking as heritage in need of urgent protection.
fact: Heritage is a noun, and when a word has several meanings, the context shows you which one fits.
exercise: «The Ukrainian Carpathians have old beech forests, part of a World Heritage Site.» What does World Heritage Site suggest? | *An old, protected place that is important | A forest that was cut down for wood | A place that is always wet | A new shop for tourists
exercise: «In Zhejiang farmers have kept fish in their rice fields for over 1,200 years.» What does this show about heritage? | A rule that stops farmers growing rice | Fish that cannot live in water | A new farming trick from last year | *Something passed on for a very long time
exercise: Ella says, «My family has Polish heritage.» What does heritage mean here? | A rule about protecting forests | A soup made from beetroot | *The culture and background passed down from family | A heritage railway with old trains
test: «Heritage railway» uses heritage as an adjective. What does it mean here? | Very fast and modern | *Old and protected because it is important | Lost and never found | Something that costs a lot of money
test: What is a country's heritage? | Its money and bank notes | *Its history, traditions and buildings passed on for a long time | Its weather for one year | Its sports team results
exam: Jayden says heritage is only old things in museums. What is the best reply? | *No, it can also mean the culture and background from your family | Yes, heritage only ever means old museum objects | Yes, heritage only means the weather | No, heritage means a fast train
